title: Variables
---

<<declare $hasNote = false>>
<<declare $hasRibbon = false>>
<<declare $hasKey = false>>
<<declare $talkedToCat = false>>


===

title: Start
---



<<if visited_count("Start") == 0 and not $hasRibbon and not $hasNote>>
  <<set $talkedToCat = true>>
  Cat: A new visitor?
  Cat: Another lost soul that dropped into our land of mad?
  Cat: What are the chances you are tied to the girl in blue?
  -> What girl in blue!? 
    Lorina: Where is she?
  Cat: She is lost, but not truly gone. If you look for her, you might actually find her, soul and all.
  -> What does that mean?!
    Lorina: My sister is alive, and I am getting her out of this madland!
  Cat: Each relic tells a story, and the right one will reveal your answer.

<<elseif $hasRibbon and not $hasNote>>
    <<jump Ribbon>>

<<elseif $hasNote and not $hasRibbon>>
    <<jump Note>>

<<elseif $hasRibbon and $hasNote>>
    <<jump Key>>

<<else>>

  Cat: You only have so much time– you'd better use it wisely. 
  Cat: Before she turns like the others. 
  Cat: Everyone here was once someone else, too, you know…


      
<<endif>>


===

title: Ribbon
---
Cat: Oh…? 

Cat: And what have we here… a ribbon once belonging to the girl in blue?

Lorina: I found it by the queen’s entrance. I know that the queen took her, but the gate is locked. How do I get in?

Cat: Mm... yes, as doors tend to do when one wishes them open.

Cat: By chance, have you tried…unlocking it?

Lorina: Listen, I'm trying to save my sister. I don't have time for this!


Cat: No, you don't, and I suppose she doesn't either

<<if not $hasNote>>

  Cat: And yet, here you are asking silly questions instead of getting answers.

  Cat: You’ve already found what she left behind, but not what she lost.

  Lorina: What does that even mean?!

  Cat: It means you are still looking at the world only from your perspective.

  Cat: Sometimes to find the truth, you need to grow and shrink, and push things into existence.

<<endif>>
===

title: Note
---
Cat: A note?
Cat: It seems like she’s begun to notice what staying in this place does to a person.
Cat: Unfortunate– but necessary.
Cat: Most never even make it that far!
Cat: Awareness is a dangerous thing to have in this place.
Cat: It tends to… let's say accelerate the process.
Lorina: What process?
Cat: The one that you are desperately trying to stop.

<<if not $hasRibbon>>
  Cat: You have found what she left behind, but not what she lost.

  Lorina: What does that mean?!

  Cat: It means that she is still somewhere in between– and that window will not stay open for long.

  Cat: Perhaps you should look for her and see where she was last seen.

  Cat: It’s not often that one wanders by the queen’s palace and comes back unscathed.
  <<endif>>

===

title: Key
---
Lorina: Hey! Stop talking in circles and help me!

Cat: Help you?

Cat: You’re quick to assume that I haven't been doing that this entire time?

Lorina: Then say something useful, please?

Cat: Useful?

Cat: Is that not what I’ve been doing this whole time?

Cat: Here–

<<dropKey>>


Cat: Go, before your window closes.

===